Mesa for Windows

The Windows distribution carries Mesa's OpenGL driver in lib/mesa (opengl32.dll and
libgallium_wgl.dll), which rava loads only for -Drava.opengl=vulkan: OpenGL then runs on the
installed Vulkan driver through Mesa's Zink.

The files come unchanged from the mesa-dist-win build of Mesa 26.2.4 (MSVC, x64):
  https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/releases/tag/26.2.4
Mesa's source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/tree/mesa-26.2.4

Most of Mesa is under the MIT license; individual files carry their own SPDX identifiers, and
the license texts Mesa uses are here (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSL-1.0, SGI-B-2.0). libgallium_wgl.dll
links LLVM, which is under the Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions (LLVM).
